<title>BELGIUM: European Union inflation falls in March.</title>
<headline>European Union inflation falls in March.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS, Belgium</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union inflation fell to a 1.7 percent annual rate in March from a 2.0 percent rate in February, the bloc's statistical arm Eurostat said Monday.</p>
<p>EU inflation in March 1996 was running at 2.6 percent.</p>
<p>Nine of the trading bloc's 15 member states came in below the EU average, with the lowest inflation rates in Finland, at 0.8 percent, Sweden at 1.0 percent and France at 1.1 percent.</p>
<p>The rates were calculated using member states' indexes of consumer prices.</p>
<p>			 Mar'97 Feb'97		  Mar'97 Feb'97</p>
<p>    European Union  1.7*   2.0*   Austria	1.2*    1.5*</p>
<p>    Belgium	   1.3    2.0    Denmark	1.5     2.0</p>
<p>    Finland	   0.8    0.6    France	 1.1     1.7</p>
<p>    Germany	   1.3    1.6    Greece	 5.9     6.5</p>
<p>    Ireland	   N/A    1.7    Italy	  2.2     2.3</p>
<p>    Luxembourg	1.3    1.5    Netherlands  1.3     1.6</p>
<p>    Portugal	  2.3    2.4    Spain	  2.2*    2.5*</p>
<p>    Sweden	    1.0    1.1    Britain	1.8     2.0</p>
<p>NOTE - * denotes provisional figure.</p>
</text>
